{"title": "Google had a very good, very bad Q3", "link": "https://9to5google.com/2026/10/29/google-had-a-very-good-very-bad-q3/", "summary": "<div class=\"feat-image\"><img src=\"https://9to5google.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/4/2025/05/Google-Logo-HQ-2.jpg?quality=82&strip=all&w=1600\" /></div><p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Good morning! Today I’m reading about the <a href=\"https://www.wired.com/story/let-the-internet-die/\">death of the internet</a>, deciding whether to buy a <a href=\"https://www.apple.com/shop/buy-mac/macbook-pro-proled-xdr\">PROLED</a> or many pro LEDs, building all my IKEA furniture with <a href=\"https://www.usebygga.com/\">this step-by-step 3D app</a>, trying desperately to get into the <a href=\"https://readwise.io/books\">Readwise Books</a> early access, and playing an <a href=\"https://opencnc3d.com/\">“Enhanced 3D” Command & Conquer: Red Alert</a> on my PC.</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><em>Inbox</em> is the tech newsletter that goes beyond the news cycle. We cover the most important 9to5Google stories from the last couple of days along with a few highlights from around the web. We publish every Tuesday and Thursday, and if you like what you read, <a href=\"https://9to5google.beehiiv.com/subscribe\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\" target=\"_blank\">please subscribe</a>.</p>\n\n\n\n <a class=\"more-link\" href=\"https://9to5google.com/2026/10/29/google-had-a-very-good-very-bad-q3/#more-735009\">more…</a>", "published": "2026-10-29T02:00:00+00:00", "source": "9to5Google", "category": "subscription", "matched_entities": {}, "logged_at": "2026-10-30T16:38:10.883925+00:00", "ontology": {"repo": "SubscriptionRadar", "category": "subscription", "ontology_version": "0.1.0", "evidence_policy_ids": ["traceable_url_required", "cross_reference_required", "non_authoritative_context_only"]}}
